<title>USA: Novartis Ciba Vision unit in settlement.</title>
<headline>Novartis Ciba Vision unit in settlement.</headline>
<dateline>HARRISBURG, Pa. 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pennsylvania Attorney General Mike Fisher said on Monday that Novartis AG unit Ciba Vision Corp has reached a settlement with Pennsylvania and 25 other states in a lawsuit alleging that Ciba and other companies conspired to inflate contact lens prices.</p>
<p>Fisher said Ciba admits no wrongdoing but agreed to pay $5 million to a settlement fund, to provide rebates potentially worth up to $43 for certain consumers, and to change its distribution policy to include mail-order companies and pharmacies.</p>
<p>The lawsuit had alleged that Ciba and other companies conspired not to sell lenses through mail-order companies and pharmacies, thus artificially inflating prices.</p>
<p>The other companies have not settled, and the cases against them will go forward, Fisher said.</p>
</text>
